//! What each built-in's props are for, component by component: a sentence
//! for each prop, what it is when a call leaves it out, and what each case
//! of an enum prop means. A prop shared by many built-ins (`disabled:`, a
//! size) is declared once in [`super::builtins`]; what it does on one of
//! them is said here, so the reference's tables, `wf registry --json` and
//! the editor's hover say it of that one.
//!
//! Every prop of every built-in has a row (a test holds the two to each
//! other); a default is `""` where the prop is required or has none worth
//! saying.

/// One prop's words.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy)]
pub struct PropDoc {
    /// The component, by its qualified name (`Card.Header`).
    pub component: &'static str,
    /// The prop, without its colon; the positional one by its name.
    pub prop: &'static str,
    /// What it does, in a sentence.
    pub summary: &'static str,
    /// What it is when a call leaves it out, as a reader writes it.
    pub default: &'static str,
    /// Each case of an enum prop, and what it means here.
    pub cases: &'static [(&'static str, &'static str)],
}

